00:43:34.460 --> 00:43:36.480
for the IOT applications.

00:43:36.480 --> 00:43:41.120
So if you have any
target signal data,

00:43:41.120 --> 00:43:43.980
you can do the similar
search on the signals

00:43:43.980 --> 00:43:47.900
from the IOT devices to
find any defective devices

00:43:47.900 --> 00:43:53.390
on the IOT platform, the
kind of the use cases.

00:43:53.390 --> 00:43:54.460
So let me summarize.

00:43:54.460 --> 00:43:56.440
So you can use the--

00:43:56.440 --> 00:43:58.750
BigQuery provides the fully
managed petabyte-scale data

00:43:58.750 --> 00:43:59.790
warehouse.

00:43:59.790 --> 00:44:01.840
It provides the
economy of cloud.

00:44:01.840 --> 00:44:03.790
It's easy to use.

00:44:03.790 --> 00:44:06.790
And also the UDF,
User-Defined Function,

00:44:06.790 --> 00:44:08.840
is so useful and
powerful computing

00:44:08.840 --> 00:44:12.370
tool that could be utilized
to analyze the signatures

00:44:12.370 --> 00:44:15.430
or feature vectors of
any kind of its contents

00:44:15.430 --> 00:44:19.420
rather than using just a simple
keyword pattern matching.

00:44:19.420 --> 00:44:23.630
And you can combine the UDF with
Machine Learning Engine, or ML

00:44:23.630 --> 00:44:26.310
Engine, to extract
the signatures

00:44:26.310 --> 00:44:29.320
by using the training
data set created by humans

00:44:29.320 --> 00:44:34.030
so that you can extract the
sense or instinct of humans

00:44:34.030 --> 00:44:38.710
to realize this
smarter analytics.

00:44:38.710 --> 00:44:41.890
And these techniques,
UDF plus ML,

00:44:41.890 --> 00:44:45.610
is available for any kind
of users in the enterprise.

00:44:45.610 --> 00:44:48.250
You can allow all
the enterprise users

00:44:48.250 --> 00:44:50.740
taking advantage of the
power of the machine learning

00:44:50.740 --> 00:44:53.404
for everyday tasks.

00:44:53.404 --> 00:44:55.320
